PATCH 457: FUN_1000_b294 base-loss -- the display-object REGISTER wrapper corrupted the mission object set.
asm 0x1b294 (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00): di = word[DGROUP:0xdfbc+param_1*4] (the slot's object near-offset); register
it via b1df(word[DGROUP:di], di); on b1df success track the max side-total a29c=(a294+a296); the tail's
`rep movs es:[di],ds:[si]` has si==di (b1df leaves si=di + already zeroed the body) = a self-copy no-op.
Ghidra base-lost it: `puVar5 = slot value` used as a HOST POINTER, so b1df's TYPE key was *puVar5 (a wild
host deref -> garbage) instead of word[DGROUP:di], and the phantom `unaff_CS`/`bVar6` split the single
near-offset + dropped b1df's CF.  On the port this passed a GARBAGE type to b1df->b21d: the AZER1 mission's
9 mobile type-2 tanks were killed (type->0x13 via b2d3) and ~66 spurious type-0x10 objects spawned within
~100 ticks -- so combat never engaged and a296 never resolved.  Oracle census (engine-context RAM dump,
cr3=0xe000): the ORIGINAL keeps 80 objects incl. 9 STEERING type-2 tanks; the port at spawn matches (80
objects, 9 tanks, byte-identical tank AI-state hdg26==des30) then diverges via this base-loss.  Rebased to
the DGROUP model + pass the real type; b1df's CF via g_fist_cf.  ASM-verified vs 0x1b294-0x1b2d2.
